OL,24,ANext PageBS-SE Eng NewsCThis DayFReg TV
FL,383,380,120,260,000,100
PN,38208
SC,0008
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F382A1786702689
OL,3,CTrain derails near Lewes station with
OL,4,Creports dozens of passengers trapped
OL,6,F"I have spoken with the Secretary of
OL,7,FState for Transport (Heidi Alexander)
OL,8,Fand the rail minister (Lord Hendy of
OL,9,FRichmond Hill) who are keeping me
OL,10,Fupdated on the situation.
OL,12,F"I know many people locally will be
OL,13,Fconcerned, and the thoughts of
OL,14,Feveryone are with those affected and
OL,15,Fthe emergency services responding at
OL,16,Fthe scene."
OL,18,FJames MacCleary, the MP for Lewes,
OL,19,Fwrote in a Facebook post: "I am aware
OL,20,Fof very concerning reports of a train
OL,21,Fcrash in the Lewes area this afternoon.
OL,26,@nD@AOUtD@AOUxD@KO]{D@[OU
OL,1,W~s1x0~s1~s hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}   G8/10
